\pard\qc\cf1\b\fs40 CONTROL OF WORK LEVEL 4 ASSURANCE\par
\fs30 Audit Question Review and Proposed BAR Classification\par
\b0\cf0\fs22 Prepared for Perenco UK / PDi\par
\fs20 14 September 2026\par
\fs18 Status: Draft for technical, operational and governance approval\par
\page
\pard\ql\cf1\b\fs28 1. Document purpose\par
\b0\cf0\fs18 This paper records all 90 questions currently used across the four Control of Work Level 4 assurance forms. Every original question is shown, assigned a proposed Barrier Assurance Rating (BAR), and revised where required to support an unambiguous Yes / No / N/A response.\par
BAR allocation is proposed and must be confirmed by Perenco\u8217?s Control of Work Technical Authority, Process Safety/HSE and operational leadership before formal issue.\par
\cf1\b\fs26 2. Review outcome\par
\b0\cf0\fs18 Original questions reviewed: 90\par
Questions recommended for revision: 67\par
Questions retained: 23\par
BAR 1 \u8211? Critical: 36\par
BAR 2 \u8211? Key operational: 49\par
BAR 3 \u8211? Supporting: 5\par
\cf1\b\fs26 3. Proposed BAR definitions\par
\cf3\b BAR 1 \u8211? Critical barrier assurance\b0\cf0 : Direct prevention or mitigation of MAH, loss of containment, isolation failure, gas-testing failure, incorrect authorisation, emergency-response failure or stop-work failure.\par
\cf4\b BAR 2 \u8211? Key operational assurance\b0\cf0 : Permit quality, task planning, hazard identification, control implementation, Toolbox Talk effectiveness, supervision and procedural compliance.\par
\cf5\b BAR 3 \u8211? Supporting assurance\b0\cf0 : Administration, planning evidence, record management, document migration, workforce perception and continuous-improvement evidence.\par
\cf1\b\fs26 4. Application rules\par
\b0\cf0\fs18 \u8226? Each question should test one observable control.\line \u8226? Yes must always mean that the requirement is met.\line \u8226? No should trigger an observation and, where required, a SMART action.\line \u8226? N/A should require a reason.\line \u8226? Numbered recommended subquestions should become separate responses in the digital form.\line \u8226? BAR 1 failures should be escalated immediately under the agreed Control of Work governance.\par
\page\pard\ql\cf1\b\fs28 AUDIT FORM 1 \u8211? CONTROL OF WORK: PERMIT QUALITY\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 1. Planning:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1a\tab \cf5 BAR 3\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the activity planned to be undertaken outside the next 24 hours?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Was the activity planned with at least 24 hours\u8217? notice?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf5 RETAIN\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Has the WCC been discussed in the daily permit meeting?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Has the WCC been discussed in the daily permit meeting?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1c\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Have current ORA\u8217?s been considered, and how they may impact on the work activity or task?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Were all current Operational Risk Assessments (ORAs) reviewed before the task was authorised?\line 2. Were any ORA impacts on the task identified and addressed?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1d\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Has a work site visit been undertaken by the PA AND AA to identify the hazards associated to the task?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Did both the Performing Authority (PA) and Area Authority (AA) complete a worksite visit before WCC issue?\line 2. Were the task and worksite hazards identified during the visit?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 2. Raising a NEW WCC: What is the task?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is there a brief, clear and concise summary of scope? Has the duration of task been identified. i.e. one shift or several?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Does the WCC contain a brief, clear and task-specific scope description?\line 2. Is the expected task duration stated, including whether it spans one or several shifts?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the work location, tools and equipment described clearly and specific?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Is the exact work location clearly identified?\line 2. Are the required tools and equipment clearly identified?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2c\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Has the increased risk of error been considered and appropriate controls identified (e.g. physical verification by AA or attaching a work location label) where similar adjacent equipment is involved / non-standard equipment numbering / poorly labelled plant, or personnel unfamiliar with the worksite etc.\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Where similar, adjacent, non-standard or poorly labelled equipment could increase the risk of error, was that risk identified?\line 2. Were specific controls implemented to prevent work on the wrong equipment or at the wrong location?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2d\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  How is the team doing it? Is the method clear?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Does the WCC clearly describe the method the work party will use to complete the task?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2e\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf5 RETAIN\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the WCC SPECIFIC to the task and not generic?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Is the WCC SPECIFIC to the task and not generic?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 2f\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the work party competent and authorised to undertake the task, with evidence that relevant PCAP requirements, task-specific training, and additional competency requirements for higher-risk activities (e.g. Breaking Containment / Bolted joints)\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Is every member of the work party competent and authorised for the assigned task?\line 2. Do PCAP records confirm the required competence?\line 3. For higher-risk work, has the required task-specific training and competence been verified?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 3. Issuing a Routine WCC:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 3a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the Routine WCC used for individual, low risk and regularly performed activities?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Is the Routine WCC limited to one clearly defined activity?\line 2. Is the activity demonstrably low risk?\line 3. Is the activity performed regularly?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 3b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Does the description of the task comply with question 2? and appropriate for the task?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Does the Routine WCC contain a clear, task-specific description that meets the requirements in Section 2?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 3c\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Does the activity involve breaking of containment on ANY system? And has a thorough hazard identification been conducted to evaluate the associated risks?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Where the activity involves breaking containment, has the correct WCC type and supplementary risk assessment been used?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 4. Identifying the Correct WCC:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 4a\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Has the correct Type of WCC been selected appropriate for the task (Cold work, BOC etc)? Has the correct risk assessment level been selected (Level 1 low risk / level 2 higher risk) appropriate to the task?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Has the correct WCC type been selected for the task?\line 2. Has the correct risk-assessment level been selected for the task risk?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 4b\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Where identified hazards require supplementary risk evaluation (BOC Checks, COSHH, HAVS, Manual handling, etc), have these been completed?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Where supplementary risk evaluation is required, has each applicable assessment been completed and referenced on the WCC?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 5. Level 2 Risk Assessment:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 5a\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Has a team consisting of 3 persons (who have suitable knowledge of the task) taken part in the risk assessment? Is the task risk assessment team leader competent (check PCAP profile)?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Did at least three people with suitable task knowledge participate in the Level 2 risk assessment?\line 2. Is the risk-assessment team leader competent, as confirmed by the PCAP profile?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 6. Risk Assessment - Task Steps:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 6a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the task broken down into to clearly defined task steps on the WCC and details the sequence in which it will be done?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Is the task broken into clearly defined steps on the WCC?\line 2. Are the steps listed in the correct working sequence?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 7. Clear Hazard Identification Statements:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 7a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is it clear What the hazard is and who/what might be harmed? Is there Only one hazard per statement?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Does each hazard statement clearly identify the hazard?\line 2. Does each statement identify who or what could be harmed?\line 3. Does each statement contain only one hazard?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 8. Clear Control Statements:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 8a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf5 RETAIN\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Are Control Statements clear on Who is doing what and when?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Are Control Statements clear on Who is doing what and when?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 8b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is there enough detail to make it clear but short and concise? Is it clear and simple language?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Does each control statement contain enough detail to be understood and implemented?\line 2. Is each control statement concise and written in plain language?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 9. Control Effectiveness:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 9a\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the risk reduction credible? Have considerations been made to ensure that for those who have been given numerous actions, the risk of error is not increased?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Does the selected control provide a credible reduction in risk?\line 2. Where individuals have numerous actions, has the increased risk of human error been assessed and controlled?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 10. Hierarchy of Controls:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 10a\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the focus towards the higher level of control, i.e. \u8220?elimination\u8221? and \u8220?substitution\u8221? rather than the lower end of the hierarchy i.e. procedures, PPE.\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Were elimination and substitution considered before relying on administrative controls or PPE?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 11. Low Value Hazard & Controls (avoiding Clutter):\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 11a\tab \cf5 BAR 3\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the WCC free from hazards and controls which do not actively reduce the risk OR are part of standardised measures already in place i.e. standards / Standard PPE etc.\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Does the WCC contain only task-specific hazards and controls that materially reduce risk?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 11b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Are the controls capable of verifying and proving the risk gap has been closed and not vague using words such as 'decide' or 'consider' or 'if required'.\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Is each control written as a specific and verifiable action?\line 2. Are vague terms such as \u8220?decide\u8221?, \u8220?consider\u8221? and \u8220?if required\u8221? avoided?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 12. Isolation Requirements:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 12a\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Have all controls within the ICC been acknowledged and transferred to the WCC?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Have all applicable ICC controls been accurately transferred to the WCC?\line 2. Has the Performing Authority acknowledged each transferred control?\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 13. Low Risk Tasks which do not require a WCC:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 13a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf5 RETAIN\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Is the site actively monitored to ensure tasks are not being undertaken without an appropriate WCC?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Is the site actively monitored to ensure tasks are not being undertaken without an appropriate WCC?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 13b\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  And, for those non-permit tasks, is a toolbox talk completed?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Where a task does not require a WCC, was a Toolbox Talk completed before work started?\par\page\pard\ql\cf1\b\fs28 AUDIT FORM 2 \u8211? TOOLBOX TALK AND PERMIT COMPLIANCE\par\pard\cf2\b\fs23\keepn 1. TBT Hazard Identification: Join the TBT and confirm that the following discussions have taken place:\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1a\tab \cf4 BAR 2\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  TBT Lead (typically the PA) discusses the hazards and controls associated to the task/activity (sourced from the Task Risk Assessment), as well as:\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Did the TBT Lead discuss the task hazards and controls identified in the Task Risk Assessment?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1b\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  SIMOP activities that may conflict with the activity / task?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  Were potential SIMOPS conflicts with the task identified and discussed?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1c\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Spills, and potential proximity to open drains discussed and how they can be avoided?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Were spill and open-drain proximity hazards discussed where relevant?\line 2. Were effective controls agreed to prevent a spill entering an open drain?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1d\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa30\cf0\b\fs17 Original:\b0  Situation awareness, such as potential dropped objects (tools, equipment or structural) discussed and actions taken?\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa100\cf0\b\fs17 Recommended:\b0  1. Were potential dropped-object and other situational hazards discussed?\line 2. Were the required controls and actions agreed before work started?\par\pard\sa80\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw8\brdrcf1\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw4\brdrcf6\cf1\b\fs19 1e\tab \cf3 BAR 1\tab \cf4 REVISED\par
